  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "Suppose `work review G --work U` sends the clean read's bundle, the branch read owner refuses it, and the fallback to the critic also fails before the work's brief is frozen. This happens when both calls hit the same transient error early in the owner (endpoint or branch-tip trouble, a failed fast gate, an unreadable record). commitReview then replaces the next step with `metasystem work review --commit U --goal G` and drops the work's `--brief`. That command dispatches the committed critic with only the generic code-read brief. The unit's accepted implementation brief is missing, so the critic cannot check conformance to the brief. Before this unit, the work form always passed `--brief BuildBrief`. The same replacement also loses the promotion after a purely transient double failure: the clean read would have been recorded if the same command were repeated, but the suggested command never sends a bundle. The brief asked only that the next step not repeat the refused command. It did not ask to drop the brief that certifies the work.",
      "evidence": "Traced in reviewed tree fd737874. intent_unit_review.go:611-627: on error with --unit-read, args becomes fallback[0], which carries `--brief BuildBrief --join` (lines 301-304), and branchRead runs again. If that also errors, the deferred function sets out.next to publicArgv(\"work\",\"review\",\"--commit\",unit,\"--goal\",goalID) without --brief whenever out.next equals sameCommand(). Every error branch at lines 714-728 returns next: inv.sameCommand(). intent_delivery.go:1186-1211 reviewCommit adds --brief only when the operator supplied one. read.go:711-712 calls branchReadBriefWithRepository with supplied nil, and read.go:282-284 then leaves out the 'Supplied accepted implementation brief' section. The record's saved brief is reused only when an earlier dispatch had already frozen it (record.DispatchRetryable, read.go:698-710), which is not the case when the failure comes before the dispatch. The commit's own test pins this next step: TestUnitReviewRecordsThePromotedReadRefusalDoesNotRepeat asserts want = publicArgv(\"work\",\"review\",\"--commit\",\"commit\",\"--goal\",id), with no --brief, and it passed in the focused run.",
      "id": "F-1-fallback-next-drops-brief",
      "material": true,
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The owner can push the unit-read Goal-Read through Commit/CommitRead and then fail to save its read record. If that save fails outright, the caller treats the error as a refusal and falls back to dispatching a critic for a version that already carries a unit-read attestation. A later collection then adds a second Goal-Read, because installedBranchRead exempts unit-read. If the save is only of unknown durability, the fallback reports already-collected but sets readNotPromoted, so the data mislabels a promoted read. This needs a local disk write failure. It is outside the default threat model's operator mistakes, and I have no reproduction.",
      "evidence": "read.go:622-631 (commit, then saveBranchReadRecord returns an error); intent_unit_review.go:613-617 (any error with --unit-read triggers the critic fallback). Traced only.",
      "id": "N-1-partial-commit-then-fallback",
      "material": false,
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "claim": "When the read is promoted, an operator's `work review G --work U --model X` (asking for a critic on model X) still sends --model with --unit-read. The owner's unit-read path ignores it, so the requested critic model is silently dropped. The brief does not address --model, so this is recorded only.",
      "evidence": "intent_unit_review.go:289-291 appends --model to the shared args; read.go:597-631 never reads request.Model on the unit-read path.",
      "id": "N-2-model-flag-ignored-on-promotion",
      "material": false,
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "claim": "When the owner refuses the bundle, readNotPromoted holds the owner's whole error text. That text can include its remedy line, e.g. 'run: metasystem work review G'. The --json data then names a remedy that is the work command itself. The next step itself is not affected.",
      "evidence": "intent_unit_review.go:616 sets reason := err.Error(); read.go:591 refusal text ends 'run: metasystem work review %s'.",
